-- title:
--   Unit translate of lattices iff isomorphic pairs (W,kerψ)
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1/\kappa$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve all of whose $q'$-torsion points vanish (hypothesis `hss`). Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule that is an order (contains $1$, is multiplicatively closed, $\mathbb{Q}$-spans the algebra, and is finitely generated) and is maximal among orders, and let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring homomorphism from `rationalEndSubring κ X₁` — the subring of $\operatorname{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the additive maps that are zero or given by rational functions outside a finite set — onto $\Lambda_1$ as a set. Fix a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$. For $i=1,2$ let $W_i$ be elliptic, $\chi_i:X_1\to W_i$ a nonzero rational homomorphism and $d_i\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ with $\theta_1$ carrying the set of endomorphisms of the form $\rho\circ\chi_i$ ($\rho$ rational, $W_i\to X_1$) onto $\mathrm{star}(d_i\cdot\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,x)$; let $W_i'$ be elliptic, $\psi_i:W_i\to W_i'$ and $\psi_i':W_i'\to W_i$ rational with $\psi_i'\circ\psi_i=N_i\cdot\mathrm{id}$, $\psi_i\circ\psi_i'=N_i\cdot\mathrm{id}$, $q'\nmid N_i$, $\#\ker\psi_i=N_i$, and let $J_i$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule with $\theta_1$ carrying the endomorphisms of the form $\rho\circ\psi_i\circ\chi_i$ ($\rho$ rational, $W_i'\to X_1$) onto $\mathrm{star}(d_i\cdot J_i)$. Then there exists $\delta\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ such that $x^{-1}\,\mathrm{finiteIdeleDiagonal}(\delta)\,x$ stabilises the finite adelic box of $\Lambda_1$ and $J_2=\delta\cdot J_1$, if and only if there are rational homomorphisms $\iota:W_1\to W_2$ and $\iota':W_2\to W_1$ with $\iota'\circ\iota=\mathrm{id}$, $\iota\circ\iota'=\mathrm{id}$ and $\ker\psi_2=\iota(\ker\psi_1)$.
--
--   This is the injectivity–faithfulness step in the Deuring–Waterhouse dictionary between left ideal classes of a maximal order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q'$ and supersingular elliptic curves over $\kappa$ equipped with a cyclic kernel of order prime to $q'$: two realisations of the same finite idèle $x$ give lattices differing by a unit of the relevant order precisely when the associated pairs (curve, kernel of the auxiliary isogeny) are isomorphic. It is used in the construction of the bijection between the quaternionic class set and supersingular places with the prescribed kernel data.
